QuestGuidance.Register("en",99,{
[3137]="70058431\n1\tTalk to Eywind near the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks\tEywind is somewhere near Caivád Sâr as the War of Three Peaks continues.\n2\tConvince dwarves to evacuate the north-eastern road targeted by Eywind (total: 6)\tSome dwarves remain dangerously close to the path where Eywind has set his stolen goblin-bombs! Eywind will not evacuate them, so it falls to you.\n3\tReturn to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks\tEywind is south of the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr, and you should return to him quickly. You do not know how long his goblin-bombs will remain undetonated.\n4\tTalk to Eywind south of Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks\tEywind is south of Caivád Sâr, admiring his handiwork.\n5\tEywind's satisfaction has turned to displeasure: for some reason not all of the bombs exploded. Did goblin-sappers recover some of the bombs, and do they now plan to use them against the dwarves? You should try and recover these twice-stolen goblin-bombs, while there is still time. Goblin-sneaks can be found in Eywind's vicinity near Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks.\t\n6\tRecover twice-stolen goblin-bombs from goblin sneaks (2/3)\tEywind's satisfaction has turned to displeasure: for some reason not all of the bombs exploded. Did goblin-sappers recover some of the bombs, and do they now plan to use them against the dwarves? You should try and recover these twice-stolen goblin-bombs, while there is still time. Goblin-sneaks can be found in Eywind's vicinity near Caivád Sâr during the War of Three Peaks.\n7\tFind and quench the hidden goblin-bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench\tThe goblin-sneak probably set his stolen bomb somewhere near the lakeside trench to the south-west, hoping to do as much damage to the dwarves as possible. You have to find and defuse it as quickly as you can!\n8\tTalk to Eywind in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks\tEywind is in the lakeside trench during the War of Three Peaks.\n9\tTalk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tDurin is inside Zarkul-sulûn while the War of Three Peaks continues.\n",
[3138]="70065D13\n1\tFind Orgolas in his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.\n2\tTalk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.\n3\tGather your thoughts concerning Golasgil\tYou try to gather your thoughts and tell Orgolas what he needs to hear.\n4\tConsider your memory of Golasgil in Minas Tirith before the siege of the White City\tYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.\n5\tConsider your memory of Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the battle\tYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.\n6\tConsider your memory of Golasgil during the Battle of the Black Gate\tYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.\n7\tWait for Orgolas to consider what you have told him\tOrgolas considers what you have told him of his father Golasgil, who perished at the Black Gate of Mordor.\n8\tTalk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.\n9\tTalk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion, and he has made up his mind.\n10\tTalk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n",
[3139]="70058430\n1\tBlow the signal horn outside Zarkul-sulûn\tDurin asked you to use the signal horn outside Zarkul-sulûn to rally the dwarves for his assault upon the threshold of Gundabad.\n2\tBlow the signal horn in one of the trenches to the north-west of Zarkul-sulûn\tDurin asked you to use the signal horn at one of the trenches to the north-west of Zarkul-sulûn to rally the dwarves for his assault upon the threshold of Gundabad.\n3\tBlow the signal horn in the hidden cave of Drenghól, the nearest encampment to Gundabad\tDurin asked you to use the signal horn at the hidden cave of Drenghól, nearest encampment to the Mountain-home, to rally the dwarves for his assault upon the threshold of Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Bróin inside the hidden cave of Drenghól\tBróin is in the hidden cave of Drenghól, nearest dwarf-encampment to Gundabad.\n5\tTalk to Bori outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tBori is outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks.\n",
[3140]="70065D14\n1\tTalk to Queen Arwen at Lond Cirion\030Talk to Ioreth at Lond Cirion\030Talk to Grethril at Lond Cirion\030Talk to Aphadaer at Lond Cirion\030Talk to Glindor at Lond Cirion\030Talk to Líniel at Lond Cirion\tYou should speak with the members of the travelling party who will leave Anfalas in the company of King Elessar.\n2\tTalk to Lady Marra outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n4\tReturn to the library of Lond Cirion inside the keep\tCaebar waits for you in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.\n5\tTalk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion\tCaebar is in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.\n",
[3141]="7005843C\n1\tTalk to Bori outside Zarkul-sulûn and go with him to confront the Lord of Gundabad\tBori is outside Zarkul-sulûn, eager to follow after Durin's assault up the steps. Can victory be close at hand?\n2\tTalk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tDurin is inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, still reeling from the events of his assault on the steps before Gundabad.\n",
[3142]="7001424E\n1\tTalk to Sweina\tSweina is somewhere among the Silvertine Lodes, likely at the southernmost reach of their mining tracks, near the entrance to the Water-works. Bósi has asked that you seek out and rescue one of his dwarves who has foolishly decided to challenge the goblins of the Silvertine Lodes. Sweina believes that the goblins of Gamil Filik have their home much deeper than the Silvertine Lodes, near the entrance to the Water-works.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You found Sweina and fought alongside him against many goblins, and should return now to Bósi.\n",
[3143]="7001AC58\n1\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.\n2\tDestroy the relic of Gorothúl in Nalâ-dûm\tThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria. Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy. He also recommends you bring an ally or two.\n3\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi.\n",
[3144]="700266E7\n1\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.\n2\tTalk to Bósi and travel to Water-works of Nalâ-dûm\tThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria. Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy.\n3\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi. You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[3145]="70018F0C\n1\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads near Durin's Way, in Moria. Gimli has asked you to travel back to Moria to speak with Bósi and to tell him that you will help the Iron Garrison with their distressing problems.\n2\tTalk to Orvar\tOrvar Bellhammer is in Buzun-ghâr, the newly-excavated passage off Durin's Way, located in the southern wall of Tharâkh Bazân's south-eastern corner. Tharâkh Bazân is to the north-east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Bósi has asked you to help Orvar, the dwarf working most closely with the Elves sent by Celeborn to Moria.\n3\tTalk to Corunothiel\tCorunothiel is at the camp inside Buzun-ghâr, located off Durin's Way in the south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân. Orvar has expressed his frustration with the Elves that have been sent by Celeborn, and wants you to speak with one of them about his irritation.\n",
[3146]="7005AFFB\n1\tIron-folk can be found on the field near Durin's Stone. Dáin has asked you to command the Iron-folk and send them to aid his father at the gates of Khazad-dûm.\t\n2\tTalk to Dáin and confront 'The Lord of Moria'\tDáin can be found at Durin's Stone. You have ordered the Iron-folk to aid Náin Orcsfoe at the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.\n3\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Muru Azog\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Muru Azog at Azanulbizar. After the defeat of Azog, Hermáth Stormhammer interjects and calls your attention to events at Muru Azog. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[3147]="70014751\n1\tTalk to Lenglammel at the Shadowed Refuge\tThe Shadowed Refuge is among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek. Galadriel sent word to Haldir that if you would save the dwarves in Moria, you must work together with the Elves she sent to the Foundations of Stone to face some great evil.\n",
[3148]="70047B59\n1\tTalk to Merry\tYou should meet Merry and Pippin at the Foothold in Udûn.\n2\tTalk to Golodhon\tGolodhon, Merry, and Pippin can be found in the Foothold camp in Udûn. You should talk to Golodhon when you are ready to head back into Mordor.\n3\tTalk to Merry\030Talk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Merry and Pippin again in Bâr Thorenion, now that you are all safely returned from Mordor.\n",
[3149]="70013AF6\n1\tDefeat deep-claws or cave-claws in the Great Delving (total: 14)\030Search Katûb-zahar for the secret to opening Nâr-khelab\tKatûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, is on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin. Bori has asked you to return to Katûb-zahar to search for some sign of the trick to opening the door to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire.\n2\tBring the rotting pages to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Command, the room up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have uncovered some pages that reveal information about Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire.\n",
[3150]="70025378\n1\tRead the letter on the crate by Halbarad in Lhanuch\tThe mysterious letter is on a crate by Halbarad. Radanir found a letter addressed 'To the Rangers' stuck in a tree with a knife, and Halbarad wants you to read it and give your opinion on its truthfulness.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch. You have read the note from Ergothorn and should now speak with Halbarad about it.\n3\tFind the entrance to Lhaid Ogo, in the Lich Bluffs\tLhaid Ogo is on the right side of the road that runs through the Lich Bluffs. Halbarad is not certain that Ergothorn can be trusted, but he wants you to travel to Lhaid Ogo to see if there is any truth to the mysterious letter. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n4\tSearch Lhaid Ogo for the lost Dunlending messenger\tSomewhere inside Lhaid Ogo, a messenger from Dunland may be in trouble. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an Inspired Greatness bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n5\tTalk to Glynn Brenin in Lhanuch\tGlynn Brenin is in the Brenin's Hall, atop the hill of Lhanuch. You have rescued the Dunlending messenger and should return to Glynn Brenin to hear his message.\n",
[3151]="7001A97B\n1\tTalk to Dúndurion at Audaghaim\tDúndurion is at Audaghaim, outside the Haunted Inn, overlooking the view from the cliffs. Cúcheron has decided to send you to Dúndurion to aid the Golden Host with their military matters while the Hidden Guard decides on a course of action.\n2\tComplete Skirmish: Strike Against Dannenglor\tThe ruins of Dannenglor are the location for a planned strike by Dúndurion. Dúndurion has asked you to participate in the strike against the merrevail-occupied ruins of Dannenglor. This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.\n3\tTalk to Dúndurion at Audaghaim\tDúndurion is at Audaghaim, outside the Haunted Inn, overlooking the view from the cliffs. You have participated in the successful strike against Dannenglor and should return now to Dúndurion.\n4\tTalk to Cúcheron outside the Haunted Inn\tCúcheron is on the front porch of the Haunted Inn, at Audaghaim. Dúndurion has sent you back to Cúcheron. Perhaps the Hidden Guard have decided what course to take on the next leg of their journey.\n",
[3152]="7005A6A5\n1\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n2\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n3\tCollect ales (total: 8)\030Collect bread (total: 8)\030Collect draughts (total: 8)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should collect some draughts, ales, and bread in Vérnozal.\n4\tPack up all the items into a care package\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should pack up all the items into a care package in Vérnozal.\n5\tCollect the care package\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should collect the care package in Vérnozal.\n6\tGive the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should give the care package to the visiting Longbeard emissary in Vérnozal.\n7\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3153]="70020996\n1\tTalk to Halros in the Greenfields\tHalros has a camp in the Greenfields, west of Bree-land, in the Shire. Saeradan has told you where to find the Ranger Halros and has warned you that Halros may find it difficult to leave the Shire, even for so important an errand.\n2\tDeal with the trouble-maker in the Green Hill Country\030Deal with the trouble-maker in Stock\tTrouble-makers can be found on the road through Green Hill Country, and in the village of Stock, in the Shire. Halros has asked you to walk the road through Green Hill Country and to visit the town of Stock to deal with the bold trouble-makers that have appeared there.\n3\tTalk to Halros in the Greenfields\tHalros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire. You have discouraged the trouble-makers in the Green Hill Country and Stock, as Halros asked, and should return now to the Ranger.\n4\tHalros has a camp in the Greenfields, in the north-east corner of the Shire. Halros has asked for your help in making the decision whether to travel south with the Grey Company or to maintain his vigil over the Shire.\t\n",
[3154]="70014644\n1\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have helped the dwarves in the Heart of Fire to prepare the defence, and Stóthkell wants you to do the same for the dwarves of the Twenty-first Hall.\n",
[3155]="700472AF\n1\tTalk to Malthengil by King Elessar's throne\tKing Elessar's guard Malthengil is near the throne.\n2\tTalk to Malthengil and witness the pronouncements of King Elessar\tKing Elessar is about to pronounce his judgements on a number of important matters, and his guard Malthengil has offered that you be allowed to watch.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3156]="7000F0F6\n1\tCollect Prepared Lunch\tDwarf-workers can be found north of Bósi's encampment, all along the winding road that runs up to the Hollin Gate. Bósi has asked you to deliver lunches to the dwarves charged with unearthing the rubble in front of the Hollin Gate, and to then report to Wárr.\n2\tTalk to Wárr\tThe dwarf Wárr is at the Hollin Gate, supervising the workers there. Now that you have delivered the lunches to the dwarf-workers along the road to the Hollin Gate, you should speak with Wárr for further engagement.\n3\tBring broken pick-axes to Bósi\tBósi is overseeing some of the waggons near the banks of the dried-up Sirannon, south of the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate. Wárr has asked you to deliver a supply of broken pick-axes to Bósi and to request replacements.\n",
[3157]="7002161C\n1\tTalk to Halbarad at the stables in Rivendell\tHalbarad is at the stables of Rivendell. Candaith has asked you to speak with Halbarad to see if he has any final words before you join the rest of the Rangers on their ride south.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at Gwingris, in Eregion, after riding south\tThe Grey Company begins its ride south. Halbarad has determined that the Rangers will rest at Gwingris, in Eregion. You should ride south to Gwingris, either on your own mount or on one engaged from Rivendell.\n3\tFind Londan the farrier and talk to him\tLondan should still be in Eregion. He left Gwingris heading east. Saeradan has asked you to find the farrier Londan and convince him to return to Gwingris so that he may repair Erebrandir's shoe.\n4\tTalk to Londan the farrier, who will be waiting for you back at Gwingris\tLondan the farrier will be waiting for you back at Gwingris, in Eregion. You have rescued Londan from the Sharkúnakh uruks that he encountered and should return to Gwingris.\n5\tTalk to Saeradan at Gwingris\tSaeradan is at Gwingris, in Eregion. The farrier Londan has thanked you for your aid, and he has asked you to speak with Saeradan.\n",
[3158]="7001466A\n1\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. Brogur has asked you to consult Bósi for some idea of what to do next, now that the dwarves have lost much of their hope of victory in Moria.\n",
[3159]="70049547\n1\tTalk to Lady Galadriel\tYou should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tYou should ask Legolas about the nature of the request he has for you.\n3\tTalk to Lady Galadriel\tYou should talk to Galadriel once more before you go.\n4\tVisit Certhíril in Mirobel\tLady Galadriel suggested you begin by visiting Certhíril in Mirobel and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.\n5\tVisit Glorfindel's spot in Rivendell\tLook for Glorfindel, or his disciple, at his accustomed spot in Rivendell, below Elrond's House and above the waterfall.\n6\tSeek Dorthaneth near Edhellond\tSeek Dorthaneth in the caves of the Avorrim, near Edhellond, in Belfalas, and ask her about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.\n7\tSeek Dorongur in Duillond\tDorthaneth suggested that Dorongor, in Duillond, might know something of what Glorfindel seeks and where he has gone. You should ask him about that and also a gift of seeds.\n8\tSeek Gildor in Tham Giliath\tDorongur has suggested that you travel to the library in Lin Giliath and look for Gildor Inglorion, whom you can ask about Glorfindel and a gift of seeds.\n9\tCheck the book-shelves (total: 6)\tGildor has suggested you look around Tham Giliath for a clue as to what Glorfindel found.\n10\tShow the record to Gildor\tYou should show the record that you found to Gildor in Tham Giliath.\n11\tDeliver the seeds to Legolas\tReturn to Legolas in the Court of Lothlórien with the many gifts of seed.\n12\tShow the record to Lady Galadriel\tNow you should show the record you found in Tham Giliath to Lady Galadriel.\n",
[3160]="70047290\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n2\tFind the missing dwarf heroes in Dor Amarth, in Mordor\tThe dwarf heroes sent into Mordor by King Thorin have not reported back in some time, and are missing somewhere in Dor Amarth, south of Lûghash. King Thorin has sent you to find the missing dwarf heroes in Mordor.\n3\tTalk to Dómor south of Lûghash, in Dor Amarth\tYou found Dómor in Dor Amarth. Does he know where the other dwarf heroes have gone?\n4\tSearch to the north for Mogi\030Search near the road for Mogi\030Search near the base of Lûghash for Mogi\tDómor asked you to search to the north, in the direction of Lûghash, for the treacherous Mogi.\n5\tTalk to Dómor south of Lûghash, near the road\tDómor has gone to the road south of Lûghash. Did he find Mogi?\n6\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n",
[3161]="7004CE9A\n1\tTalk to Gwedhir south-west of the ruins of Díngarth\tGwedhir is south-west of the ruins of Díngarth, in Dor Amarth. Mithrandir asked you to find Gwedhir in Dor Amarth and hear his report.\n2\tTalk to Harthalín west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith\tHarthalín is west of Faltor Gâm, in Agarnaith. Mithrandir asked you to find Harthalín in Agarnaith and hear her report.\n3\tTalk to Thenca south of Agarnaith, along the road in Talath Úrui\tThenca is south of Agarnaith, by the road in Talath Úrui. Mithrandir asked you to find Thenca in Talath Úrui and hear his report.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n",
[3162]="700599EC\n1\tTalk to Glóin outside Zarkul-sulûn\tGlóin stands outside Zarkul-sulûn, watching as more dwarves arrive for the conquest of the Mountain-home.\n2\tMeet with the new arrivals outside Zarkul-sulûn\tGlóin expressed his surprise and dismay at the artists and craftsmen that have answered Durin's call and come to Zarkul-sulûn. You should speak with these new arrivals and learn why they have come to such a place of war.\n3\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer outside Zarkul-sulûn\tStáli the Hewer stands outside Zarkul-sulûn. Why has the sculptor come to such a dangerous place in time of war?\n4\tTalk to Eskil Bloodthumb outside Zarkul-sulûn\tStáli has directed you to speak to his apprentice, Eskil Bloodthumb, outside Zarkul-sulûn.\n5\tPick up some of Stáli's luggage\tStáli the Hewer has ordered that Eskil Bloodthumb carry his master's luggage to the upper floor inside Zarkul-sulûn. You have decided to help Eskil in this task, so the apprentice need not carry everything by himself.\n6\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn\tStáli the Hewer has arrived on the upper floor of Zarkul-sulûn.\n7\tTalk to Prince Ingór downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn\tPrince Ingór is downstairs in Zarkul-sulûn, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[3163]="70066287\n1\tComplete 'The Crew: Knight of the Green Hills'\030Complete 'The Crew: The Boon Companions'\030Complete 'The Crew: The Sea-longing Lord'\030Complete 'The Crew: She Who Remained'\030Complete 'The Crew: The Corsair Jajax'\030Recruit any other members of the crew you wish\tCaebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.\n2\tTalk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion when you are satisfied with your crew\030Recruit any other members of the crew you wish\tCaebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew. When you are satisfied with the crew you have assembled, return to the library of Lond Cirion and speak with Caebar.\n",
[3164]="700599EF\n1\tCollect picks and shovels from a barrel within Zarkul-sulûn\tPrince Ingór asked you to collect some picks and shovels from inside Zarkul-sulûn and deliver them to some of the Zhélruka standing idle within the fortress.\n2\tDistribute picks and shovels to idle Zhélruka inside Zarkul-sulûn (total: 3)\tIdle Zhélruka can be found throughout the fortress of Zarkul-sulûn, waiting for you to give them picks and shovels to use to break through the ice in front of Gundabad.\n3\tTalk to Prince Ingór in Zarkul-sulûn\tPrince Ingór is waiting to hear that his people have been given the supplies needed to break through the ice blocking the entrance to Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Durin in Zarkul-sulûn\tDurin is eager to gain access to Gundabad, and believes that the ice will not long stand before the combined efforts of his Longbeards and Prince Ingór's Zhélruka.\n5\tTalk to Durin and travel with him to the gates of Gundabad\tDurin is eager to gain access to Gundabad, and believes that the ice will not long stand before the combined efforts of his Longbeards and Prince Ingór's Zhélruka. When you are ready, he will go with you to the gates of Gundabad.\n6\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard\tDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, inside the mighty court of Máttugard.\n",
[3165]="700662B5\n1\tTravel to the Wave-hunter where it is docked in Pinnath Gelin\tThe Wave-hunter is docked on the lake outside Ost Arndír.\n2\tTalk to Nauriel beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin\tNauriel readies for the voyage of the Wave-hunter where the ship is docked in Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tTalk to Sigileth beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath Gelin\tSigileth readies for the departure of the Wave-hunter.\n4\tTalk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunter\tSirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, lost in his thoughts, as he prepares for the voyage.\n",
[3166]="7004CE9B\n1\tFind Plákash in Durthang\030Find Durkhlát outside Cirith Ungol\tPlákash can be found somewhere within Durthang. Durkhlát can be found outside Cirith Ungol. Mithrandir asked you to find one of the Orcs that seek the Weeping Warrior and compel him to divulge the purpose for his search.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n3\tFind Galadriel and Celeborn outside Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood\tLady Galadriel and Lord Celeborn have come with the Golden Host to Dol Guldur, in preparation for the fortress's destruction. You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.\n4\tTalk to Lord Celeborn outside Thangúlhad\tLady Galadriel and Lord Celeborn have come with the Golden Host to Dol Guldur, in preparation for the fortress's destruction. You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.\n5\tTalk to Lady Galadriel outside Thangúlhad\tLady Galadriel and Lord Celeborn have come with the Golden Host to Dol Guldur, in preparation for the fortress's destruction. You will find them outside the fortress of Thangúlhad in the Gathbúrz area of Southern Mirkwood.\n",
[3167]="700599F0\n1\tGlóin is north of Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard, down one level. Durin put Glóin in charge of scouting the mighty court, and asked you to aid him with his task.\t\n2\tDefeat cave-claws or deep-claws in Máttugard (total: 6)\030Defeat bats or gredbyg in Máttugard (total: 6)\030Defeat cave-beasts in Máttugard (total: 4)\030Search piles of debris for artifacts from the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs\tGlóin asked you to defeat several different enemies lurking within Máttugard, and to search for relics from the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, when last the dwarves occupied Gundabad.\n3\tBring the weapon of the Sixth War to Glóin north of Maergrind\tGlóin is north of Maergrind in Máttugard.\n",
[3168]="70066DD9\n1\tTalk to Sirgon and give the order for the ship to set sail to Umbar\tSirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, eager for the ship to set sail.\n2\tTalk to Daxamat at Voyage's End in the Shield Isles\tDaxamat has left the ship and awaits your orders.\n3\tConfront the men watching you from the tree line to the west\tSomeone watches you from the tree line to the west of the Wave-hunter.\n4\tTalk to Mattân to the west of the Wave-hunter\030Talk to Ozâl to the west of the Wave-hunter\tTwo residents of the Shield Isles watch you with suspicion in their eyes.\n5\tTalk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles\tCaebar stands by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.\n",
})
